Cancel an early ims_dialog with 500 and a CANCEL with Reason 503.

When a module asks ims_dialog to end a dialog that is still being set up
(ims_qos when the PCRF reports the media bearer lost, ims_charging, a
deregistration), dlg_terminate() answered the caller with 488 (Not
Acceptable Here) and let tm CANCEL the forwarded INVITE with that code as
its Reason. TS 24.229 5.2.8.1.1 has the P-CSCF answer the original INVITE
with 500 (Server Internal Error) and CANCEL towards the callee with a Reason
header carrying 503 (Service Unavailable) when no cause is known; 5.4.5.1.1
has the S-CSCF CANCEL and send "an appropriate response", which 500 is.

CANCEL the branches first with Reason cause 503 (the local reply would
otherwise CANCEL them with its own code), then reply 500.

Outside a SIP worker (ims_qos, ims_charging and usrloc timers) it also
called t_release() on the INVITE right after the reply, so tm dropped the
transaction: the final reply was sent once, never retransmitted, and the
caller's ACK had nothing to match. Reply with t_reply_trans() on the dialog's
transaction and leave it to tm.

